actively monitoring camera feeds.\n+\t\t\t</description>\n+\t\t</method>\n \t\t<method name=\"remove_feed\">\n \t\t\t<return type=\"void\" />\n \t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"feed\" type=\"CameraFeed\" />\n \t\t\t<description>\n \t\t\t\tRemoves the specified camera [param feed].\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"set_is_monitoring_feeds\">","path":"doc/classes/CameraServer.xml","commit_id":"54685c3037116b25093a4ab2b91e3b978dd0e06f","original_commit_id":"5d94cdc1eb41d7df74b3cf78ff7adc13025fd835","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I didn't want to bind the setter to a property, because as a user I wouldn't expect `CameraServer.monitoring_feeds = true` to cause a synchronized 120ms delay.\r\nPerhaps that's just a testament that the check should be asynchronously performed on macOS as well. Then I'd be OK with a property. Otherwise, I'd rather have functions that look like functions.\r\n\r\nThe name you suggested works for me. I'm pretty used to `set_is` names from other APIs but it's not super important to me as long as the name is unambiguous.","created_at":"2025-03-18T14:03:54Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T10:15:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2001133501","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2001133501"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2001133501"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2001133501/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":53,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2001027728,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005598396","pull_request_review_id":2702640707,"id":2005598396,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc53iwC8","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,13 +37,27 @@\n \t\t\t\tReturns the number of [CameraFeed]s registered.\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"is_monitoring_feeds\" qualifiers=\"const\">\n+\t\t\t<return type=\"bool\" />\n+\t\t\t<description>\n+\t\t\t\tReturns `true` if the server is actively monitoring camera feeds.\n+\t\t\t</description>\n+\t\t</method>\n \t\t<method name=\"remove_feed\">\n \t\t\t<return type=\"void\" />\n \t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"feed\" type=\"CameraFeed\" />\n \t\t\t<description>\n \t\t\t\tRemoves the specified camera [param feed].\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"set_is_monitoring_feeds\">","path":"doc/classes/CameraServer.xml","commit_id":"54685c3037116b25093a4ab2b91e3b978dd0e06f","original_commit_id":"5d94cdc1eb41d7df74b3cf78ff7adc13025fd835","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Alright, I added an `is_monitoring_feeds` property.\r\n\r\nI experimented with a few different names with setters and getters. `monitoring_feeds_enabled` and `set_monitoring_feeds_enabled` could generally work, but I felt very unhappy giving them a different / inconsistent word root. It's just not clear enough that they refer to the same variable. Since `is_monitoring_feeds` as a property is what we expect users to use practically, I think `get_is_monitoring_feeds` and `set_is_monitoring_feeds` are acceptable names for the getter and setter, even if they do sound a bit awkward.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you disagree. If you feel strongly about this I'm ok to give in and rename them :)","created_at":"2025-03-20T13:04:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T13:06:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2005598396","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005598396"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2005598396"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005598396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":53,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2001027728,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005686067","pull_request_review_id":2702813262,"id":2005686067,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc53jFcz","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,13 +37,27 @@\n \t\t\t\tReturns the number of [CameraFeed]s registered.\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"is_monitoring_feeds\" qualifiers=\"const\">\n+\t\t\t<return type=\"bool\" />\n+\t\t\t<description>\n+\t\t\t\tReturns `true` if the server is actively monitoring camera feeds.\n+\t\t\t</description>\n+\t\t</method>\n \t\t<method name=\"remove_feed\">\n \t\t\t<return type=\"void\" />\n \t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"feed\" type=\"CameraFeed\" />\n \t\t\t<description>\n \t\t\t\tRemoves the specified camera [param feed].\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"set_is_monitoring_feeds\">","path":"doc/classes/CameraServer.xml","commit_id":"54685c3037116b25093a4ab2b91e3b978dd0e06f","original_commit_id":"5d94cdc1eb41d7df74b3cf78ff7adc13025fd835","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Well to me a property starting with `is_` is pretty uncommon, and that's the convention we use (somewhat inconsistently) for getters of boolean properties (often with infinitive -> gerund), e.g.:\r\n```\r\nControl.auto_translate (set_auto_translate, is_auto_translating)\r\nControl.clip_contents (set_clip_contents, is_clipping_contents)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I would name the property `monitor_feeds` (`set_monitor_feeds`, `is_monitoring_feeds`) or `monitoring_feeds` if the gerund seems necessary in the property itself (`set_monitoring_feeds`, `is_monitoring_feeds`).","created_at":"2025-03-20T13:47:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T13:47:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2005686067","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005686067"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#discussion_r2005686067"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005686067/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":53,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2001027728,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.